  "worked_solution": "First, we construct the matrix $E$, whose columns are the eigenvectors ${v}_{1}$ and ${v}_{2}:$\n\n$$\nE=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 5 & 3\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nNow, the decoupling matrix can be found as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D & ={E}^{-1} \\\\  & ={[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 5 & 3\\end{aligned}]}^{-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2\\cdot 3-5\\cdot 1}[\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 \\\\ -5 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 \\\\ -5 & 2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$",
